    "chunk_size_bytes": 763,
    "chunk_text": "If the critique of that report by the CEJ is anywhere near correct, the victims of those adverse impacts might well be the settlers themselves. This could be Weli Oya over again; operational decisions made by local officials who have their own interests and are barely accountable to distant Colombo and settlers bitterly disappointed because the agricultural resources required to fulfill promises made to them are not actually available. Add to that the problem of inflamed Sinhalese-Tamil relations, potential environmental degradation and escalating the human-elephant conflict that makes daily life precarious and the potential downside to the government from proceeding with the current Kivul Oya project without more careful enquiry seems unbearably large."
  },
  {
