    "md5": "057be53d0606e0684f8ea28e708fb2cb",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1743,
    "chunk_text": "MSME recovery in post-Ditwah Sri Lanka: Turning geographic data into action\n\nIntegrating MSME geolocation into a national statistical system would improve recovery support coordination and reduce the risk of fund misallocation\n\nThis exercise uses a survey of 2,500 MSMEs conducted in January 2025 to demonstrate how a geographical database can help evaluate post-disaster exposure\n\n52.5% of surveyed MSMEs with high exposure risk demonstrated inadequate understanding of building standards, low insurance coverage, and high levels of indebtedness\n\nThe recent cyclonic storm Ditwah disrupted micro, small, and medium enterprises (MSMEs) islandwide, caused by production disruptions, infrastructure damage (including roads and mobile networks), supply-chain interruptions, and reduced access to markets. Rapid responses were necessary for the MSME sector to restart business operations and reconnect to markets. In fact, the effects of Cyclone Ditwah might amplify preexisting vulnerabilities in the MSME sector, including a heavy debt burden, informality, susceptibility to domestic demand shocks, and limited technical capacity to build climate resilience.\n\nWhile an effective and targeted response requires reliable and timely data, a key challenge in identifying impacts is the lack of a central MSME database. The systematic incorporation of geographical information (GI) into national databases is becoming increasingly important amid frequent climate-related disasters. This article demonstrates that an MSME database incorporating geocoordinates and socio-demographic data could rapidly inform policymakers and support the design of targeted response measures.\n\nRapid assessment of exposure to Ditwah using geolocation data: A case study"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-02-12-dailyftlk-4360b164",
    "num": "dailyftlk-4360b164",
    "date_str": "2026-02-12",
    "description": "MSME recovery in post-Ditwah Sri Lanka: Turning geographic data into action",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/columns/MSME-recovery-in-post-Ditwah-Sri-Lanka-Turning-geographic-data-into-action/4-788207",
    "lang": "en",
